#N canvas 20 20 3000 2760 12;
#X text 20 20 phase3-bench -- the Phase 3 acceptance run on hardware. It drives itself with 10 seconds between steps so you can watch the OLED and mark each one off. Load it as a third patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch: it only pushes onto disp err and mode., f 110;
#X text 20 110 RUN IN THE FOREGROUND. Every step prints what it is sending and a PASS IF line -- including the steps whose correct result is that NOTHING happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark. About three minutes end to end., f 110;
#X obj 2300 190 r \$0-say;
#X obj 2300 230 print;
#X obj 20 230 loadbang;
#X obj 140 300 del 6000;
#X obj 140 328 t b b b ;
#X msg 320 366 === STEP-01-of-14 === baseline -- sending nothing;
#X obj 320 396 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 366 PASS IF: two bars with a small gate mark under each and a BPM at the bottom -- Phase 5 hands the footer over from v0.2-ready to the tempo about four seconds in;
#X obj 1100 396 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 450 del 10000;
#X obj 140 478 t b b b b ;
#X msg 320 516 === STEP-02-of-14 === PARAM WITH A UNIT -- sending chop-size 43 %;
#X obj 320 546 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 516 PASS IF: chop-size on the top line and a big 43 % under it -- bars shrink to a thin strip -- then about 1.2s later the meters come back on their own;
#X obj 1100 546 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 516 chop-size 43 %;
#X obj 2300 546 s disp;
#X obj 140 600 del 10000;
#X obj 140 628 t b b b b ;
#X msg 320 666 === STEP-03-of-14 === PARAM WITH NO UNIT -- sending grain 12;
#X obj 320 696 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 666 PASS IF: grain then a big 12 and NO PERCENT SIGN left over from the last step -- this is the one that matters most;
#X obj 1100 696 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 666 grain 12;
#X obj 2300 696 s disp;
#X obj 140 750 del 10000;
#X obj 140 778 t b b b b ;
#X msg 320 816 === STEP-04-of-14 === MODAL -- sending modal recording;
#X obj 320 846 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 816 PASS IF: recording in mid-size text with the bars as a thin strip -- and unlike a param it STAYS and does not fade;
#X obj 1100 846 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 816 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 846 s disp;
#X obj 140 900 del 10000;
#X obj 140 928 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 966 === STEP-05-of-14 === PARAM WHILE A MODAL IS UP -- sending chop-size 43 %;
#X obj 320 996 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 966 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES -- still says recording and chop-size never appears -- the modal outranks it;
#X obj 1100 996 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 966 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 996 s disp;
#X msg 2620 966 chop-size 43 %;
#X obj 2620 996 s disp;
#X obj 140 1050 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1078 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1116 === STEP-06-of-14 === WARNING OVER THE MODAL -- sending warn u_root test-warn;
#X obj 320 1146 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1116 PASS IF: a box border with warn then u_root then test-warn -- AND about 2s later it vanishes and RECORDING IS BACK underneath;
#X obj 1100 1146 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1116 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1146 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1116 warn u_root test-warn;
#X obj 2620 1146 s err;
#X obj 140 1200 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1228 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1266 === STEP-07-of-14 === MODE TO PERFORM -- nothing is sent to the screen;
#X obj 320 1296 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1266 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES -- still recording. Mode is never drawn -- this only sets up the next two steps;
#X obj 1100 1296 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1266 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1296 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1266 perform;
#X obj 2620 1296 s mode;
#X obj 140 1350 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1378 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1416 === STEP-08-of-14 === WARNING WHILE IN PERFORM -- sending warn u_root hidden-warn;
#X obj 320 1446 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1416 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES -- no alert box at all -- still recording. Perform mode suppresses warnings;
#X obj 1100 1446 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1416 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1446 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1416 warn u_root hidden-warn;
#X obj 2620 1446 s err;
#X obj 140 1500 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1528 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1566 === STEP-09-of-14 === FAILURE WHILE IN PERFORM -- sending fail u_root shown-fail;
#X obj 320 1596 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1566 PASS IF: an alert DOES appear -- fail then u_root then shown-fail -- failures are never suppressed -- then recording returns after about 4s;
#X obj 1100 1596 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1566 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1596 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1566 fail u_root shown-fail;
#X obj 2620 1596 s err;
#X obj 140 1650 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1678 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1716 === STEP-10-of-14 === MODE BACK TO COMPOSE -- nothing is sent to the screen;
#X obj 320 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1716 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES -- still recording;
#X obj 1100 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1716 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1746 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1716 compose;
#X obj 2620 1746 s mode;
#X obj 140 1800 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1828 t b b b b b ;
#X msg 320 1866 === STEP-11-of-14 === WARNING NOW WE ARE BACK IN COMPOSE -- sending warn u_root back-again;
#X obj 320 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1866 PASS IF: the alert DOES appear this time -- warn then u_root then back-again -- the filter released;
#X obj 1100 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 1866 modal recording;
#X obj 2300 1896 s disp;
#X msg 2620 1866 warn u_root back-again;
#X obj 2620 1896 s err;
#X obj 140 1950 del 10000;
#X obj 140 1978 t b b b b ;
#X msg 320 2016 === STEP-12-of-14 === CLEARING THE MODAL -- sending modal-off;
#X obj 320 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2016 PASS IF: recording disappears and you are back to the two meters and the BPM footer;
#X obj 1100 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 2016 modal-off;
#X obj 2300 2046 s disp;
#X obj 140 2100 del 10000;
#X obj 140 2128 t b b b b ;
#X msg 320 2166 === STEP-13-of-14 === SAFETY TIMEOUT -- sending modal stuck and then DELIBERATELY never clearing it;
#X obj 320 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2166 PASS IF: stuck appears now -- then with NO further input it clears itself after 30s. Next line is in 35s;
#X obj 1100 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2300 2166 modal stuck;
#X obj 2300 2196 s disp;
#X obj 140 2250 del 35000;
#X obj 140 2278 t b b b ;
#X msg 320 2316 === STEP-14-of-14 === done -- press Ctrl-C;
#X obj 320 2346 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2316 PASS IF: the screen returned to the meters on its own during that 35s wait -- that was the safety timeout;
#X obj 1100 2346 s \$0-say;
#X text 20 2420 EVERY STEP RE-ASSERTS THE MODAL rather than relying on the one set in step 04 still being up. It is not: a modal carries a 30-second safety timeout \, and at 10 seconds a step the original expired exactly as step 07 fired -- which read as three failures that were really the safety net doing its job., f 110;
#X text 20 2530 Each step hands off to the next so the delays are RELATIVE. Both label lines fire BEFORE the messages do -- trigger order runs rightmost first -- so you always read what to expect before the screen moves. NO COMMAS OR SEMICOLONS in a label: both are message separators inside a message box., f 110;
